1. Scope (compute) - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) the billing basis (the proposal shows both hourly and monthly rates);
(b) whether public IP, bandwidth and firewall are included or charged extra;
(c) that the client will manage only ERP user credentials and application-level access, and that network, hypervisor, OS patching, firewall, encryption, backups and DR are managed by LeapSwitch;
(d) pricing for additional storage.

2. Disaster recovery - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) that DR is added to the Service Scope;
(b) a committed RPO of 1 hour and RTO of 4 hours;
(c) DR invocation on failure, cyber incident or the client's request, with failback without data loss;
(d) DR drills twice a year, with a written report.

3. Backup - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) daily automated, application-consistent backups;
(b) encryption, with one immutable copy;
(c) failed backups notified within 1 hour and re-run within 4 hours;
(d) quarterly test restoration.

4. Load balancer and one-time cost - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) the purpose of the load balancer line;
(b) what the one-time setup cost covers;
(c) that LeapSwitch remains responsible for its subcontractor;
(d) that no data is routed or stored outside India.

5. Security - LeapSwitch to confirm encryption at rest and in transit, MFA for admin access, access logs retained in India for 180 days, incident notification within 6 hours and a root cause analysis within 5 business days.

6. Service levels - LeapSwitch to:
(a) share the SLA, including how uptime is measured and the service credits;
(b) confirm planned maintenance only outside business hours, with prior notice;
(c) confirm response and resolution times;
(d) confirm that availability below the SLA in 2 consecutive months allows termination without charges.

7. Pricing and payment - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) prices fixed for the 12-month term;
(b) only undisputed invoices payable, disputes within 10 working days;
(c) prepaid fees refunded pro rata on our breach or force majeure.

8. Acceptance - billing to start only after a 7-day testing period.

9. Term - 12 months from acceptance, renewed automatically unless the parties agree in writing to terminate.

10. Termination - LeapSwitch to confirm:
(a) the amount of the early termination charges;
(b) that the client may terminate for convenience on 60 days' notice.

11. Suspension - only for undisputed amounts overdue by more than 30 days, after 15 days' written notice.

12. Exit - up to 60 days' transition; full data export within 7 days at no extra cost.

13. Changes - changes to backups, DR site, encryption or data centre location need the client's prior written consent.

14. Hosting location - LeapSwitch to name the primary and DR facilities.

15. Liability - cap of 12 months' fees; data restoration costs recoverable.

16. Force majeure - backup and DR to continue; either party may exit if the event continues beyond 15 days.
